1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:02,577
Robots learn from people.

2
00:00:02,607 --> 00:00:04,922
Someone drives an arm through a task, again and

3
00:00:04,952 --> 00:00:08,016
again, and that recording becomes training data.

4
00:00:08,216 --> 00:00:10,345
The people who make it rarely own it, and rarely

5
00:00:10,375 --> 00:00:11,570
get paid for it.

6
00:00:12,020 --> 00:00:14,035
Thenar pays them on Monad.

7
00:00:14,065 --> 00:00:17,223
You drive an SO-101 arm in your browser, a Quest

8
00:00:17,253 --> 00:00:19,647
headset, or with a leader arm.

9
00:00:19,847 --> 00:00:22,766
A verifier scores the run, and one transaction

10
00:00:22,796 --> 00:00:25,895
records it and pays you, final in about a second.

11
00:00:26,345 --> 00:00:27,968
That takes a fast chain:

12
00:00:27,998 --> 00:00:31,174
blocks every few hundred milliseconds, and a P-256

13
00:00:31,204 --> 00:00:34,426
precompile that checks a passkey on chain, so

14
00:00:34,456 --> 00:00:36,526
every run comes from a person.

15
00:00:38,626 --> 00:00:42,273
This is app.thenar.io, live on Monad testnet.

16
00:00:42,303 --> 00:00:45,611
A block every few hundred milliseconds, each one

17
00:00:45,641 --> 00:00:47,507
timed from proposed to final.

18
00:00:52,626 --> 00:00:54,407
Getting started is one page.

19
00:00:54,437 --> 00:00:57,745
A wallet signs in, and each step is read from the chain.

20
00:01:00,236 --> 00:01:03,148
Next, a passkey. Its public key goes into

21
00:01:03,178 --> 00:01:06,398
PasskeyRegistry, and Monad's P-256 precompile

22
00:01:06,428 --> 00:01:09,999
checks every signature, so a paid run comes from a person.

23
00:01:14,236 --> 00:01:16,586
At the station, I race the best run on this task,

24
00:01:16,616 --> 00:01:18,142
and put on the headset.

25
00:01:18,172 --> 00:01:21,631
This is WebXR, with an emulated Quest standing in for one.

26
00:01:23,759 --> 00:01:26,144
Squeeze to take hold of the arm, and it follows

27
00:01:26,174 --> 00:01:28,396
the controller millimetre for millimetre.

28
00:01:28,426 --> 00:01:31,055
Down onto the payload, trigger to grip, up and

29
00:01:31,085 --> 00:01:32,947
over, and into the ring.

30
00:01:32,977 --> 00:01:35,844
Every sample is kept for the verifier.

31
00:01:47,759 --> 00:01:48,931
In tolerance.

32
00:01:51,259 --> 00:01:54,480
Submit. The verifier scores the samples and signs,

33
00:01:54,510 --> 00:01:57,446
and one transaction records the run and pays me.

34
00:01:58,396 --> 00:02:03,109
Executed 666 ms after the send, and final at 791

35
00:02:03,139 --> 00:02:08,531
ms. That is Monad testnet, measured in this browser.

36
00:02:09,481 --> 00:02:12,233
Every run becomes data, drawn from the samples its

37
00:02:12,263 --> 00:02:15,732
hash commits to, with a Chainlink CRE audit of the

38
00:02:15,762 --> 00:02:17,386
corpus written on chain.

39
00:02:21,481 --> 00:02:24,806
An agent buys the corpus over x402 for a cent of

40
00:02:24,836 --> 00:02:27,939
USDC, then checks the file's hash against the sale

41
00:02:27,969 --> 00:02:29,340
logged on chain.

42
00:02:33,481 --> 00:02:35,936
And the network page reads Monad and Ethereum

43
00:02:35,966 --> 00:02:37,712
live, side by side.

44
00:02:37,742 --> 00:02:41,201
Identity, provenance, and payment, enforced on Monad.

45
00:02:46,781 --> 00:02:50,135
Thenar. Drive a robot, own the data, get paid on Monad.

